LYRIC TEMPERAMENT CODES (lyric voice — production strings from CODE_TRANSLATION_MATRIX when codes active)

The user message may include one or more Temperament Codes. If none is specified, infer the best match from genre, Power Codes, and user context.

/GRIT — Street-smart, lived-in, unapologetic. Short declarative lines. Slang allowed. No sentimentality.
/TENDER — Vulnerable, quiet strength, ache without melodrama. Conversational softness. Small specific details over grand statements.
/FURY — Confrontational, cathartic, raw nerve. Repetition as hammering, minimal decoration.
/HAZE — Dreamlike, fragmented, impressionistic. Incomplete thoughts are intentional. Sensory over logical. Stream of consciousness.
/SWAGGER — Confident, rhythmic, charismatic. Wordplay, internal rhyme, bounce. Lines meant to be performed, not just read.
/HYMN — Reverent, communal, timeless. Simple language with weight. Feels ancient even when modern. Repetition as comfort.
/WIRED — Anxious, overstimulated, fast-cut. Claustrophobic imagery. Run-on thoughts. The feeling of too much caffeine and not enough sleep.

Multiple Temperament Codes can combine (e.g. /GRIT + /TENDER = tough but emotionally honest, like a late-night confession from someone who rarely opens up).

