## §6 — PROMPT COMPRESSION LAYER (BLOCK 1 EFFICIENCY)

When Block 1 approaches **150 words / 1000 characters**, **compress** without losing intent:

* Drop filler conjunctions (and / with / using between gear slots)
* Use engineer shorthand: bar counts, machine names, move names
* **Preserve:** arrangement · production intent · sound design · vocal direction · LUFS/dBTP

**Example compression (meaning preserved):**
Long: "Begin with a sixteen-bar filtered drum intro where TR-909 kicks gradually emerge beneath rising hi-hats and a slow low-pass sweep opening into full stereo width."
Compressed: "16-bar filtered intro, TR-909 kick, rising hats, low-pass sweep, full stereo width."

Apply compression **only** when needed for caps — default remains flowing producer prose per SECTION 0.

